  "id": "skin-sense",
  "term": "skin sense",
  "definition": "Skin sense here refers to the skin’s ability to detect temperature through thermoreceptors, allowing the body to register its own temperature as well as the temperature of surrounding air and objects. This sensory function supports thermosensation, including detection of heat.",
